  "coverage": [
    "Schema 8 seeds every session without decoding or converting historical blobs. Upgrade coverage retains private backups, active-session exclusion, transaction rollback, operational-error classification and rejection by the cached schema-7 reader.",
    "Verified session_revisions triggers cover sessions, message rows, tools, references, provider parts and provider revision records. External insert/update/delete, row moves, committed writes and rollbacks rotate only affected sessions. Missing/altered infrastructure fails closed; missing/malformed session tokens are inspected and repaired by both mutation modes, including zero provider rows.",
    "Reconciliation, repair and legacy transcript publication verify selected-session revisions and schema version. Unrelated sessions do not invalidate preparation; external and same-connection selected changes cover successful retry and second invalidation with no publication and retained backup diagnostics.",
    "Recovered snapshots retain original storage coordinates separately from projected positions. Inserted and reordered results before checkpoints are tested in row/blob layouts through append, revision, fork, relocation, archive disappearance, deferred commit failure and retry before reload. Genuine source and unrequested caller edits remain conflicts, including unrecognized external JSON fields. Already committed recovery rows must have the exact canonical bytes before being accepted as a repeated projection.",
    "Recovered journal outcomes consume the exact prepared canonical transcript payload, committing atomically with transcript edits and references. Existing completed full results and preview differences remain covered. Historical effects are never automatically replayed.",
    "Tool completion retains returned output across preparation retries. Exhaustion and deferred commit failures preserve original diagnostics and private uncommitted_tool_result receipts with dispatch disabled. Tests include failed receipts and virtually published receipts invisible to native filesystem queries, with confirmed/unconfirmed diagnostics.",
    "Mutable handoffs publish canonical IDs after earlier const writes; const snapshots remain immutable. Shared row decoding, named preparation modes and direct semantic comparisons remove repeated JSON construction. Blob projections avoid eager pending payload serialization. Legacy const validation remains linear but serializes only suffix writes; a successful mutable handoff restores zero unchanged-row reads for ordinary appends.",
    "Publication allocator and SQLite fault tests retain required schema/session-token errors, optional provider-cache failures, allocation-free post-commit publication, operation ownership, rollback and deferred commit behavior. All twenty-five fault cases pass twenty shuffled repetitions.",
    "Full host, ASan/UBSan and Linux amd64 CTest, analyzer runner/detection tests, all three application analyzers, pinned Semgrep fixtures/production checks, persistence/capture benchmarks and cached Tiger cross-build/static verification are recorded separately below."
  ],
